<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        Whether this account's password has to be replaced before the account can be used.

        WHY IT IS A COLUMN
        The question is about provenance: a password chosen by the person it belongs to, or one that was set for
        them. Nothing about the credential itself records that, and a client cannot be trusted to remember it, so
        it is remembered here — the same reasoning as the lock and the idle stamp, and it survives a restart.

        WHEN IT IS SET, AND WHY THAT MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS
        It is set when an account is created by somebody else, whose password this application generates and nobody
        ever sees. It is cleared when the person sets a password of their own, and that includes the reset link they
        use to reach their account for the first time — without that, every account created by a Super Admin would
        be refused everything for ever, which is a lockout dressed as a policy.

        WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE TODAY
        The account is unusable between creation and that first password either way, because the generated password
        is not communicated to anybody. So this closes the door on a case that does not yet exist: an administrator
        setting a password and handing it over. If that is ever added, this is the control that already covers it.

        EXISTING ACCOUNTS
        Defaults to false, so every account that exists now keeps working exactly as it does, and nobody is asked to
        change a password they chose themselves.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20261005100000-1" author="hms">
        <comment>Add jhi_user.password_change_required for the forced first-login password change</comment>
        <addColumn tableName="jhi_user">
            <column
                name="password_change_required"
                type="boolean"
                defaultValueBoolean="false"
                remarks="Set when a password was chosen for this account rather than by it; cleared when the account sets its own">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
